// `Eq` is total, structural value equality, modeled on Swift's `Equatable`.
//
// A managed `struct` or `sum` satisfies `Eq` by listing `derives(Eq)` (or
// `derives(Ord)`, which implies `Eq`), which the compiler expands into a
// structural equality over every field. The builtin equatable scalars
// (`Int`, `String`, `Bool`, ...) satisfy `Eq` directly. `Eq` is a pure,
// total contract: it introduces no mutation, retention, native, or unsafe
// boundary.
protocol Eq {
    fn equals(self: Self, other: Self) -> Bool
}
